WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:03.269
Britain's military intelligence

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:04.637
believes that Russian attacks

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:06.706
are gaining more traction in backing.

00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:07.741
The Ukrainian military released

00:00:07.741 --> 00:00:08.408
this video

00:00:08.408 --> 00:00:10.176
showing troops fighting House-to-house

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:11.111
in damaged buildings.

00:00:11.111 --> 00:00:12.779
But British intelligence says

00:00:12.779 --> 00:00:14.147
it believes the Russian troops

00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:14.581
have, quote,

00:00:14.581 --> 00:00:16.416
regained some momentum there

00:00:16.416 --> 00:00:17.584
and have likely advanced

00:00:17.584 --> 00:00:18.785
into the city center.

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:19.853
Meanwhile, Ukrainian

00:00:19.853 --> 00:00:21.054
officials are making it clear

00:00:21.054 --> 00:00:21.888
that they're not ready

00:00:21.888 --> 00:00:23.690
for any territorial concessions

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:24.591
to Russia.

00:00:24.591 --> 00:00:25.058
That appears

00:00:25.058 --> 00:00:26.126
to walk back remarks

00:00:26.126 --> 00:00:27.594
from a top presidential adviser

00:00:27.594 --> 00:00:29.362
who suggested to the Financial Times

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:32.265
that Crimea could be up for negotiation.

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:34.167
The Ukrainian aircraft producer

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:36.002
wants to get the world's largest plane

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:37.404
back in the sky.

00:00:37.404 --> 00:00:39.939
Antonov 25 was one of a kind

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:41.775
which Ukraine built in the 1980s.

00:00:41.775 --> 00:00:43.176
It was an engineering marvel

00:00:43.176 --> 00:00:44.277
before it was destroyed

00:00:44.277 --> 00:00:46.112
in the early days of the war.

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:48.615
But as David McKenzie reports, Ukraine is

00:00:48.615 --> 00:00:49.816
not ready to give up on it.

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:54.754
The first hours of the war,

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:55.922
Russian elite forces

00:00:55.922 --> 00:00:56.623
descending on

00:00:56.623 --> 00:00:58.658
just the more airport outside Kiev,

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:02.062
their intended launch pad to the capital

00:01:03.963 --> 00:01:05.298
It didn't work out.

00:01:05.298 --> 00:01:06.366
Ukrainian forces

00:01:06.366 --> 00:01:08.868
famously pushed the Russians back

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:10.703
and they made a discovery at them.

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:12.872
All the pride of Ukraine.

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:13.807
The remarkable

00:01:13.807 --> 00:01:16.709
And two to five or Maria cargo plane

00:01:17.077 --> 00:01:18.611
gutted in the fighting.

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:20.980
You know, it was feeling like

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:24.717
you are a part of something great.

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:26.553
It's the first time

00:01:26.553 --> 00:01:28.988
pilot Yevgeny Kaczynski has come back.

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:31.324
Yevgeny coming back here,

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:33.760
it must be quite hard for you

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:36.830
What's the emotion like?

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:40.500
It's very, very hard to be here

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:44.104
and to see all this station's

00:01:44.337 --> 00:01:47.107
destroyed plane destroyed hangars.

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:49.142
It's quite hard to see.

00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:50.043
The Ukrainian

00:01:50.043 --> 00:01:51.044
Antonov company

00:01:51.044 --> 00:01:52.679
says it wants to rebuild this

00:01:52.679 --> 00:01:54.214
one of a kind giant.

00:01:54.214 --> 00:01:56.116
No matter what it takes

00:01:56.116 --> 00:01:57.250
or not, bring more.

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:58.151
Designer Valeria

00:01:58.151 --> 00:01:59.119
Castillo says

00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:00.420
they've already retrieved

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:02.188
much of what they can use.

00:02:02.188 --> 00:02:04.591
You can feel the extraordinary size

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:06.926
of this plane inside the fuselage.

00:02:06.926 --> 00:02:09.195
The Maria was the heaviest plane

00:02:09.195 --> 00:02:09.796
in the world

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:13.399
and it could carry up to 250 tons inside

00:02:13.666 --> 00:02:14.701
or even on top,

00:02:15.735 --> 00:02:16.436
designed to

00:02:16.436 --> 00:02:17.704
transport the Soviet

00:02:17.704 --> 00:02:19.906
era Buren spacecraft.

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:22.075
The Antonov company refurbished the Maria

00:02:22.075 --> 00:02:25.645
multiple times with six TurboFan engines,

00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:28.648
each with more than £50,000 of thrust

00:02:29.015 --> 00:02:31.184
and a 32 wheel landing gear system.

00:02:31.451 --> 00:02:34.420
The Maria was a marvel, an outsized hit

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:35.021
with plane

00:02:35.021 --> 00:02:37.624
spotters and aviation enthusiasts.

00:02:37.924 --> 00:02:39.225
When you were flying this plane,

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:41.127
so many people wanted to take photos

00:02:41.127 --> 00:02:42.862
of it, follow it.

00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:44.831
What was that like?

00:02:45.265 --> 00:02:47.700
I was feeling a

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:49.903
great responsibility,

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:54.407
not only to operate this plane

00:02:54.807 --> 00:02:56.943
properly, correctly,

00:02:56.943 --> 00:02:59.512
but it was also a great responsibility

00:02:59.512 --> 00:03:01.381
because you're attracting

00:03:01.381 --> 00:03:02.682
a lot of attention.

00:03:02.682 --> 00:03:04.784
A few days after,

00:03:04.784 --> 00:03:07.287
you can open the YouTube and see

00:03:07.554 --> 00:03:10.423
all what have done.

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:12.825
But to put Maria back in the sky,

00:03:12.825 --> 00:03:14.060
the Antonov company says

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:16.262
it could cost nearly $1,000,000,000

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:17.530
and take years.

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:18.631
But for Ukrainians,

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:20.700
it's a point of pride.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:23.069
David McKenzie CNN, Kiev, Ukraine.

00:03:24.003 --> 00:03:24.571
A Moscow

00:03:24.571 --> 00:03:25.205
court has set a

00:03:25.205 --> 00:03:25.905
date to hear

00:03:25.905 --> 00:03:27.240
an appeal of the arrest

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:28.374
of an American journalist.

00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:30.376
That is according to Russian state media,

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:32.011
which cited the court

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:32.612
Evan Gersh

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:33.680
Kovic is a reporter

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:34.781
for The Wall Street Journal,

00:03:34.781 --> 00:03:36.583
and he faces up to 20 years

00:03:36.583 --> 00:03:38.618
in prison on espionage charges.

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:40.086
The Journal vehemently denied

00:03:40.086 --> 00:03:41.421
the charges, calling it a quote,

00:03:41.421 --> 00:03:43.456
vicious affront to a free press.

00:03:43.756 --> 00:03:45.391
The court will hear the appeal on April

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:46.292
the 18th.

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:47.093
His arrest marks

00:03:47.093 --> 00:03:48.228
a significant escalation

00:03:48.228 --> 00:03:50.096
of both Moscow's tensions with the U.S.

00:03:50.096 --> 00:03:51.030
and its campaign

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:52.465
against foreign news media.

